---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const title = "Privacy & Data Protection";
const description = "How Vision Hub demos handle camera data, consent, and integrity in compliance with EU and Swedish law.";
---

<SiteLayout {title} {description}>
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:800px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 16px;">
    <h1>Privacy & Data Protection</h1>

    <p>
      This page describes how <b>Vision Hub</b> processes visual data in compliance with the
      <b>European Union’s General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, Regulation (EU) 2016/679)</b>
      and Sweden’s national implementation, <b>Dataskyddsförordningen</b>.
      The system follows the integrity principles defined by
      <b>Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten (IMY)</b>, Sweden’s data protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Purpose of the demonstration</h2>
    <p>
      The Vision Hub installation at Luleå University of Technology showcases interactive
      <b>AI-based computer vision models</b> that operate in real time. The purpose is purely
      educational and research-oriented — to demonstrate how modern AI systems can detect
      objects, track movement, or estimate human poses visually.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Type of data processed</h2>
    <p>
      The demo processes <b>live video frames</b> from a fixed camera connected to the installation.
      These frames are analyzed instantly in memory to draw overlays (such as boxes or skeletons)
      on a live screen.  
      <u>No videos, images, or identifying information are ever recorded, saved, or transmitted.</u>
    </p>

    <p>
      Once you step out of view or the demo resets, all visual data is discarded immediately.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Legal basis for processing</h2>
    <p>
      The visual processing is based on <b>Article 6(1)(a) of the GDPR</b> — your
      <b>explicit consent</b> to participate in a live, camera-based AI demonstration.
      The processing serves no commercial or surveillance purpose.
    </p>

    <p>
      Participation is entirely voluntary. You may withdraw consent at any time by asking
      a staff member to stop the demo or by stepping away from the camera area.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Consent management</h2>
    <p>
      When a visitor gives consent to participate, a short-lived <b>consent token</b> is created
      within the <b>local demo environment</b> (on the lab’s computer).  
      This token:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Is valid for approximately 10 minutes.</li>
      <li>Contains no personal or identifying data.</li>
      <li>Is used only to temporarily authorize the live demo.</li>
      <li>Expires automatically and is not stored anywhere after the session.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The consent is therefore <b>entirely local to the installation</b> and cannot be accessed
      or linked to any external system, individual, or network.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data retention and storage</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No image, audio, or video data is stored or transmitted.</li>
      <li>No identifiers such as IP addresses, cookies, or session IDs are collected.</li>
      <li>The system does not log any personal activity, face, or biometric pattern.</li>
      <li>All AI processing occurs in real time and in memory only.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The demo computer is isolated within the lab network and used solely for on-site research
      and exhibition purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights under EU and Swedish law</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR and Swedish Data Protection Act, you have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Be informed about how visual data is used.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent at any time.</li>
      <li>Request erasure or restriction of any personal data (not applicable here, as none is stored).</li>
      <li>Contact <b>Integritetsskyddsmyndigheten (IMY)</b> if you believe your rights are violated.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Since no data is stored or transferred, withdrawing consent simply ends the live session.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Contact information</h2>
    <p>
      For any question about data protection and privacy in Vision Hub, please contact:
    </p>

    <p>
      <b>Tom Burellier</b><br/>
      Vision Hub Project – Luleå University of Technology<br/>
      Email: <a href="mailto:tom.burellier@telecom-sudparis.eu">tom.burellier@telecom-sudparis.eu</a>
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:32px;color:#9cb0d8;font-size:0.9rem;">
      Last updated: October 2025 — compliant with the EU GDPR and Swedish Data Protection Act (Dataskyddsförordningen).
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- /src/pages/privacy.astro (inside <SiteLayout>) -->
<link rel="modulepreload" href="/scripts/consent-widget.js" />
<script type="module" src="/scripts/consent-widget.js"></script>

<h1>Privacy & Consent</h1>
<p class="sub">This demo setup uses short-lived local consent tokens. You can see and withdraw them below.</p>

<!-- Configure via attributes -->
<consent-status
  demos="yolo,pose"
  orch=":8090"
  token="dev-token"
  stop="true"
  intro="Below is your consent status on this station. Tokens are short-lived and stored locally. You can withdraw at any time."
></consent-status>
</SiteLayout>
